    "raw_text": "FIRST INFORMATION REPORT (F.I.R.)\nUnder Section 154 Cr.P.C.\nPolice Station: Special Crime Branch, New Delhi\nFIR No: 204/2026\nDate and Time of FIR: October 22, 2026 at 02:30 AM\nInvestigating Officer: Inspector Alok Verma, Badge SCB-109\n\n1. DETAILS OF OCCURRENCE:\n   Date: October 21, 2026\n   Time: Approximately 11:30 PM\n   Place of Occurrence: Connaught Bank High-Security Vault, Barakhamba Road, New Delhi\n\n2. BRIEF FACTS OF COMPLAINT:\n   On October 21, 2026 at around 11:45 PM, an automated emergency seismic alarm was triggered in Vault Room B of Connaught Bank. Responding patrol team Unit-4 arrived at the facility at 11:58 PM.\n   Upon entry, Bank Vault Custodian Suresh Menon was discovered restrained and unconscious on the vault floor. Preliminary inspection confirmed that cryptographic security hardware and ₹4.5 Crore in bearer financial securities belonging to Apex Global Securities were stolen.\n   A PCR mobile patrol van stationed near Outer Ring Road reported that three suspects were spotted fleeing the rear service alley in a dark car with tinted windows heading east towards Noida.\n   The incident has been classified as high-priority corporate sabotage and grand larceny under Sections 380, 420, and 120-B of the Indian Penal Code.\n",
