    "raw_text": "WITNESS EXAMINATION & RECORDED TESTIMONY\nCriminal Case: Connaught Bank Vault Heist (FIR No: 204/2026)\nDate of Statement: October 22, 2026 at 09:00 AM\nWitness Name: Rameshwar Lal\nOccupation: Senior Security Supervisor, ShieldPro Security Services\nLocation of Examination: Special Crime Branch Headquarters, New Delhi\n\nSWORN TESTIMONY:\nI, Rameshwar Lal, state under oath:\nOn the night of October 21, 2026, I was assigned to the perimeter security desk at Gate 3 of Connaught Bank on Barakhamba Road. My duty shift commenced at 08:00 PM and was scheduled to conclude at 08:00 AM.\nAt approximately 11:15 PM, I performed the mandatory physical inspection of the loading docks adjacent to Vault Room B. The electronic mag-locks appeared secure.\nHowever, at approximately 11:45 PM, I was alerted by a sharp metallic impact from the rear service bay. I immediately proceeded towards the loading ramp with a flashlight.\nI saw two men wearing black tactical jumpsuits and balaclavas carrying aluminum payload cases. The suspects loaded the metal cases into a white van parked near Gate 3.\nThe driver of the vehicle gunned the engine and escaped at high speed towards Tolstoy Marg. The license plate was partially obscured by mud, but the white van bore commercial fleet markings.\nI immediately engaged the silent panic button to summon the central police dispatch.\n",
