    "raw_text": "CENTRAL CYBER FORENSICS LABORATORY (CCFL)\nDIGITAL EVIDENCE EXTRACTION & SERVER AUDIT REPORT\nReport ID: CCFL-DEL-2026-8812\nSubject: Connaught Bank Core Infrastructure Intrusion\nTarget Vault: Vault Room B Cryptographic HSM\nDate of Examination: October 22, 2026 at 06:00 PM\nChief Examiner: Dr. Ananya Sen, Principal Forensic Specialist\nEXECUTIVE SUMMARY:\nOn October 21, 2026 at 11:40 PM, the multi-factor authentication lock guarding Vault Room B was\ncompromised.\nThe intruder authenticated directly from the local physical maintenance console located inside Connaught\nBank.\nCRITICAL DIGITAL ARTIFACTS:\n1. Authentication Token: Account credentials belonging to Vikram Malhotra (Employee ID: VM-8821) were\nutilized to authorize the vault door override.\n2. Cryptographic Key Transfer: At 11:42 PM, master decryption keys for Apex Global Securities bearer\nassets were copied onto an unencrypted SanDisk USB drive.\n3. Access Point: The physical terminal located 5 meters outside Vault Room B was accessed with\nbiometric fingerprint validation of Vikram Malhotra.\n4. Telecommunication Tower Dump: Cell phone number +91-98110-44219 assigned to Vikram Malhotra\nwas registered pinging the Barakhamba Road cellular cell tower from 10:50 PM on October 21, 2026 until\n12:05 AM on October 22, 2026, completely disproving his presence at Hotel Oberoi during the robbery.\nCONCLUSION:\nThe digital evidence incontrovertibly establishes that Vikram Malhotra was physically present inside\nConnaught Bank on October 21, 2026 during the vault penetration.",
